  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="transcription" xml:id="transcription_aad_0166" xml:lang="en">
          <div type="letter">
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00505/" ed="1r" type="sheet"/>
            <div type="letter_message" hand="#type_black_ede_ravenscroft">
              <opener>
                <seg hand="#print_ede_ravenscroft">
                  <lb/>TELEPHONE: 01-405 0602
                </seg>
                <seg hand="#print_ede_ravenscroft">
                  <lb/>TELEGRAMS: EDE, 01-405 0602
                  <lb/>CABLEGRAMS: EAGLEHAWK-LONDON
                </seg>
                <seg hand="#print_ede_ravenscroft">
                  <lb/><rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_356">EDE, &amp; RAVENSCROFT LTD</rs>
                  <lb/>H. M. WALTON, J. F. AUSTIN, L. WALTON, F. W. BIRCH, J. DURRANT
                  <lb/>FOUNDED IN THE REIGN OF <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_552">WILLIAM</rs> &amp; <rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_553">MARY</rs> 1689.
                </seg>
                <seg hand="#print_ede_ravenscroft">  
                  <lb/>ROBE MAKERS &amp; TAILORS
                  <lb/>93 &amp; 94 CHANCERY LANE <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_56">LONDON</rs> W C 2
                </seg>
                <seg hand="#print_ede_ravenscroft">  
                  <lb/>COURT, DIPLOMATIC &amp; PRIVATE CLOTHES,
                  <lb/>PEERS, ACADEMIC, LEGAL &amp; MUNICIPAL ROBES.
                </seg>
                <seg hand="#print_ede_ravenscroft">  
                  <lb/>LAW WIGS<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>UNIFORMS
                </seg>
                <seg hand="#print_ede_ravenscroft">  
                  <lb/>THE FIRM HAS BEEN THE RECOGNISED AUTHORITY ON COURT DRESS AND ROBES FOR UPWARDS OF 275 YEARS.
                </seg> 
                <seg>
                  <lb/>JFA/BC
                </seg>
                <dateline>  
                  <date>
                    <lb/><space quantity="44" unit="char"/>28th April, l970.
                  </date>
                </dateline>
                <seg>
                  <persName>
                    <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">W. H. Auden</rs>, Esq.,
                  </persName>
                  <placeName>
                    <address>
                        <lb/><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_5">Kirchstetten,
                        <lb/><foreign xml:lang="de">Bezirk</foreign> Street. <rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_9">Polten</rs>,
                        <lb/><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_2">Hinterholz 6</rs>,
                        <lb/><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_6">NO.O.</rs> 
                        <lb/><rs type="place" ref="#amp_place_id_10">Austria</rs>.</rs>
                    </address>
                  </placeName>
                </seg>
                <salute>
                  <lb/><rs type="person" ref="#amp_person_1">Sir</rs>,
                </salute>
              </opener>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="11" unit="char"/>Being the Official Robemakers to the <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_358">University of Sheffield</rs>,
                <lb/>they have informed us that you are to have <rs type="event" ref="#amp_event_id_302">conferred upon you the
                <lb/>Honorary Degree of D.Litt.</rs>
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="11" unit="char"/>We write to ask if we may have the honour of supplying you
                <lb/>with new robes, on the other hand, you may only wish to have hired
                <lb/>Robes for the <rs type="event" ref="#amp_event_id_302">Degree Ceremony</rs>, in which case the <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_358">University</rs> will
                <lb/>supply. <space quantity="1" unit="char"/>In either case the robes will be ready for you in the
                <lb/>appropriate Robing Room on the day of the Ceremony.
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="11" unit="char"/>The cost of new D.Litt Robes, would
                <lb/><space quantity="11" unit="char"/>be:-
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="12" unit="char"/>Gown in fine lightweight all wool Panama.......&#163;33.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>0.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>0.
                <lb/><space quantity="12" unit="char"/>Hood - Art Silk lined Silk Taffeta.............&#163; 7.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>7.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>0.
                <lb/><space quantity="12" unit="char"/>Hat - Velvet Mortar Board......................&#163; 6.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>2.<space quantity="2" unit="char"/>0. 
              </p>
              <p>
                <lb/><space quantity="11" unit="char"/>Should we be favoured with your order it would be appreciated
                <lb/>if you would let us have your full height and hat size.
              </p>
              <closer>
                <salute>
                  <lb/><space quantity="11" unit="char"/>Assuring you of our best and personal attention at all
                  <lb/>times,
                </salute>
                <salute>
                  <lb/><space quantity="44" unit="char"/>We are, Sir,
                  <lb/><space quantity="44" unit="char"/>Your obedient servants,
                </salute>
                <signed>
                  <lb/><space quantity="39" unit="char"/>p.p. <rs type="org" ref="#amp_organization_356">EDE &amp; RAVENSCROFT, LTD.</rs>,
                </signed>
                <signed hand="#hand_blue_unident_0166_01">
                  <lb/>J.<unclear>F.A.</unclear>
                </signed>
              </closer>
            </div>                
        <pb facs="https://iiif.acdh.oeaw.ac.at/aad/aad_00506/" ed="1v" type="sheet"/>
            <div>
              <ab hand="#hand_blue_unident_0166_02">
                <lb/>18
              </ab>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
    </body>
